---
title: Salsa Macha
servings: 1
tags:
  - condiment
source:
  name: Ricky Bayless
  url: https://www.rickbayless.com/recipe/salsa-macha-3/
-- introduction: 
---

Heat @garlic{75%gram}(smashed) @neutral oil{1%cup} in a #skillet{} (make sure it is sized so that the oil pools enough to cover the garlic and chilies, approximately 0.5 inches deep)\
> Try to keep the oil temp below 275 deg F.

When @garlic{} begins to brown, add @dried chilies{40%gram}.\
> Have a mix of chilies like arbol, chipotle, guajillo, etc. Remove stems from them, and pith and seeds to reduce spice and bitterness if you want.

Add @nuts{60%gram}(chopped) to the mixture and let roast for ~{2%min} (don't let it burn).\
> Use a mix of pumpkin seeds, peanut, seasame seeds, or anything else you like. You can also use ground versions of these too (like peanut butter or tahini) if that's easier, you won't have the crunch from the bigger pieces though.

Add @balsamic vinegar{1.5%tbsp} and salt to taste.
> Can use a different vinegar as well, just need a little acid for balance.

Let the oil mixture cool until room temperature, then blend to desired consistency.